WEBVTT

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:03.880
Welcome, welcome!

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:06.770
Great deals on shiroma, itou, and mamashu today!

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:07.750
How's that for ya?

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.380
Welcome, welcome!

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:17.230
<i>Oshutoru ordered us on a supply transport mission,</i>

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:18.510
<i>so we left the capital.</i>

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.270
<i>During our maritime voyage to Tusukuru, we stopped at Shahhoro,</i>

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:26.520
<i>the port town ruled by Atui's father, Soyankekuru.</i>

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:31.560
It's overflowing with juiciness!

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.200
So refreshing!

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.630
It's delicious.

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:37.990
It's so hot.

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:39.780
Like a steam bath...

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:46.040
Isn't it good?

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:46.860
It's great!

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:52.550
What's that?

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:02.640
An assassin?

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:09.060
Atui!

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:09.940
Yah!

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:18.990
Huh?

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:54.290
Atui! Atui! Atui!

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:56.080
How've you been?

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:58.050
Rub, rub, rub, rub!

00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:01.480
Oh how I've missed this feeling!

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.930
Atui! Atui!

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:06.600
Wh-What's going on?

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.880
That there is Atui-sama's father.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:11.820
You mean, he's one of the Eight Pillar Generals?

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:12.440
Yes.

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:14.310
You must've been <i>so</i> lonely.

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:17.440
You don't need to go anywhere ever again.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:19.320
Rub, rub, rub, rub!

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:22.700
Pops, your beard's all itchy! It hurts y'know!

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:25.870
What a moving reunion between father and daughter!

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:27.110
Shinonon!

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:31.190
So you're Haku-kun?

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:33.240
I am Soyankekuru,

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:36.080
father of the lovely Atui.

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:40.510
I'm told you've been taking care of Atui in the capital.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:42.840
For that, I offer my thanks.

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:46.970
No, thank you.

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:50.980
Thank you for bringing these supplies here.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:56.420
I'll ferry you all to Tusukuru myself.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.920
Now, getting to the point...

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:06.590
What exactly is your relationship with my Atui?

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:09.240
Mister?

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:13.850
He's a special man to me.

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:14.750
A <i>special</i> man?

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:21.890
So close we are, there ain't a thing we gotta keep secret between us.

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:25.940
We've stayed up all night talkin' many a time.

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:29.270
<i>All</i> night, you say?

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:32.480
Y-You seem to have the wrong idea...

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:34.140
Come to think of it,

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:37.760
don't you spend a lot of time going out at night with Atui?

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:41.070
Hey, you're leaving out some important words!

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:42.630
Personal servant.

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:45.840
From morning to night, ever by his side.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:47.470
How filthy.

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:48.660
Haku-kun...

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:53.170
I see you're taking <i>very</i> good care of my daughter.

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:59.290
W-We just went out drinking all night!

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:01.800
Atui and I aren't like that!

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:02.800
Of course.

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:04.820
Of <i>course</i> you aren't like that.

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:10.680
Well, how about we have a little chat about <i>all</i> the details once we're aboard?

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.330
It's not like tha—

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:12.810
Ow!

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:28.690
The loading's complete.

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:30.240
Ready to depart, on your command.

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:33.300
Depart!

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:34.920
Our destination is Tusukuru!

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:36.080
Weigh anchor!

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:48.270
It's wonderful to watch men who know their roles so well.

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:54.510
I can see why my father considers 
Soyankekuru of the Unlit Seas his rival.

00:05:54.510 --> 00:05:57.230
Everyone's outfits are so nice, too!

00:05:57.230 --> 00:05:59.980
Hearin' you all say that makes me happy.

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:04.880
Back in the day, everyone'd just loiter 'round in their underwear. Wouldn't even bathe.

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:07.350
Always cussin' and whatnot, too.

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:09.490
I'd had enough.

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:13.480
So I made the whole lot of 'em wash up,

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:15.620
clean up their language,

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:20.190
and got 'em fashionable clothes from the capital, too.

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:25.250
But I must've done somethin' wrong.

00:06:26.470 --> 00:06:29.570
It all feels a bit off...

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:35.370
Maybe those outfits are only meant for pretty boys?

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:55.370
So cute!

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:57.780
They're welcomin' you, Ruru-yan.

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:02.670
How strange.

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:08.400
By my calculations, a ship of this size shouldn't be sailing this smoothly.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:12.400
Perhaps it's some ancient magic.

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:17.700
How much of the stories about ancient magic do you think is true?

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:20.060
Carriages that ran without horses,

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:23.570
giant snakes that swallowed people and carried them to faraway destinations,

00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:25.670
iron birds that flew in the skies,

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:27.130
Haku-kun!

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:27.950
and ships that sailed the sea of stars...

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:29.250
It's <i>really</i> not like that!

00:07:27.950 --> 00:07:29.940
I find it hard to believe any of those tales.

00:07:31.030 --> 00:07:34.220
But the more research I do,

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:37.450
the more it seems that they're no mere fairy tales.

00:07:38.670 --> 00:07:39.510
Yes.

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:46.330
The invasion of Tusukuru is the will of the Emperor.

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:49.840
We can fight for the people of Yamato once more.

00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:55.090
I shall complete my mission, even if it costs me my life!

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:02.710
I suspected this might happen,

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:06.600
so I had Kuon-san prepare some medicine for seasickness.

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:08.610
Medicine...

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:18.870
What a persistent old guy...

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:21.390
He wouldn't even listen to me.

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:28.130
Kuon?

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:36.010
Kuon?

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:37.390
Haku...

00:08:38.190 --> 00:08:39.860
So this is where you were.

00:08:42.260 --> 00:08:43.460
Where are the others?

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:44.950
Resting inside.

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:47.420
Sailing is new to them, so they're tired.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:48.650
I see.

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:51.800
It's so quiet.

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:52.650
Yeah.

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:55.650
Are you sure about this?

00:08:57.360 --> 00:08:58.830
We're going to Tusukuru.

00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:02.000
You'll be fighting your own people.

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:05.750
If you're doing this for my sake...

00:09:05.750 --> 00:09:06.660
No.

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:09.660
I'm not.

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:11.210
I want to go.

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:15.420
If they fight head-on, Yamato will lose.

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:19.670
If that happens, Atui, Rurutie, and the others...

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:24.110
I have to end this war, one way or another.

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:28.850
<i>And I'm the only one who can.</i>

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:30.810
Kuon...

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:34.440
Actually...

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:36.160
It's nothing.

00:09:39.310 --> 00:09:42.150
People can be such a pain.

00:09:43.090 --> 00:09:43.960
Yeah.

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:55.210
I can see land!

00:09:55.940 --> 00:09:57.970
Land ho!

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:06.980
Tusukuru...

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:22.150
Land!

00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:26.090
Land, my mother! Land, my father!

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:29.820
I thank you for allowing my safe return!

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:34.080
I love the feel of stepping on land with my own two feet.

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:38.130
People were never meant to leave land!

00:10:34.510 --> 00:10:36.280
Can't say I blame her.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:39.420
Her seasickness just about killed her.

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:42.140
Nosuri-sama, I'm so glad for you.

00:10:43.060 --> 00:10:43.890
Now, then...

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:46.520
Where's Munechika's camp?

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:48.730
According to the map made in Yamato,

00:10:48.730 --> 00:10:52.400
our present location is this coast, here.

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:55.780
And Munechika-sama's camp is here.

00:10:56.570 --> 00:11:00.010
They're locked in a stalemate with the Tusukuru forces.

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:05.910
There's only one road. 
A long one, with no forks or cover...

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:09.560
We'd be inviting them to attack.

00:11:10.470 --> 00:11:11.920
There is another path.

00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:14.900
Only the locals know of it.

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:17.000
It's steep and rough,

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:21.080
but there's less chance of being found than if we take the main road.

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:25.180
Then, if you've made your decision, shall we move out?

00:11:25.180 --> 00:11:27.930
Y-You're goin' too, Pops?

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:32.060
Of course, my precious Atui.

00:11:32.590 --> 00:11:34.690
We're entering enemy territory.

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:38.320
I can't let you be put in danger.

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:42.780
Pops... I appreciate the sentiment,

00:11:42.780 --> 00:11:44.950
but you should stay put.

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:49.050
You're worried about my ship?

00:11:49.050 --> 00:11:52.280
You really are such a kind girl.

00:11:52.280 --> 00:11:53.870
Fear not!

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:57.030
Raikou's forces are at the port,

00:11:57.030 --> 00:12:01.210
so I can accompany you worry free.

00:12:01.210 --> 00:12:03.940
That ain't what I meant!

00:12:03.940 --> 00:12:06.340
You think I'm getting too old to fight?

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:09.680
I may not look it,

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:12.100
but I'm one of the 
Eight Pillar Generals for a reason.

00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:16.350
I still train daily!

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:21.500
Muscles, everywhere...

00:12:22.890 --> 00:12:24.340
Soyankekuru-san...

00:12:25.210 --> 00:12:28.480
Our mission is to deliver the supplies.

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:32.270
We don't want to draw attention by bringing too many people.

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:34.100
But...

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:35.620
Don't you worry.

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:38.450
I'm your daughter, Pops.

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:41.630
I ain't losin' to the likes of them Tusukuru soldiers.

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:43.260
Atui!

00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:48.970
Is this what it means for a daughter to grow up!?

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:51.010
Shinonon!

00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:52.980
Haku-kun!

00:12:52.980 --> 00:12:54.770
Take care of my daughter.

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:57.610
I'm sure you understand this, but...

00:12:58.370 --> 00:13:00.860
Should <i>anything</i> happen to Atui,

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:03.740
I'll be holding <i>you</i> responsible.

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:05.530
Keep that in mind.

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:07.010
<i>His eyes aren't smiling.</i>

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:08.670
<i>They're not smiling at all!</i>

00:13:41.310 --> 00:13:44.520
I'm glad my big sister knew about this path.

00:13:44.520 --> 00:13:47.570
I don't think the enemy'll find us now.

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:51.790
How much farther up does this hill go?

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:54.100
Just a bit.

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:56.360
Once we get to the top, it's downhill for a while.

00:13:56.360 --> 00:13:57.390
Just hang in there.

00:14:01.850 --> 00:14:03.920
What's wrong, Kokopo?

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:12.510
What's wrong, Kokopo?

00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:13.920
What's goin' on?

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:15.420
Did something happen?

00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:16.930
Kokopo?

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:25.070
There's nothing there...

00:14:36.470 --> 00:14:37.960
Master Haku!

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:46.710
Mukkuru...

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:11.830
Big Sister!

00:15:11.830 --> 00:15:13.850
M-Master Haku...

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:15.130
Wh-What do we do?

00:15:15.130 --> 00:15:16.300
Do we keep going forward?

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:25.500
<i>So that's their plan...</i>

00:15:35.610 --> 00:15:36.590
What's wrong?

00:15:36.590 --> 00:15:37.390
That's...

00:15:40.900 --> 00:15:42.120
Munechika-sama!

00:16:05.420 --> 00:16:07.230
That's Master Haku.

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:09.720
Open the gate! Immediately!

00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:10.300
Yes, ma'am.

00:16:21.770 --> 00:16:24.440
I-It finally stopped...

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:26.440
We're saved.

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:32.750
Let's go.

00:16:41.570 --> 00:16:42.450
Master Haku!

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:43.700
Munechika?

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:47.300
Does that mean this is Yamato's main camp?

00:16:47.300 --> 00:16:47.960
Indeed.

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:52.280
But what are you all doing here?

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:56.090
Oshutoru-sama asked us to bring supplies.

00:16:57.530 --> 00:17:00.570
This is all we've got left, though.

00:17:01.300 --> 00:17:04.850
No, even this much is welcome.

00:17:21.450 --> 00:17:22.200
Meat!

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:23.120
It's meat!

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:25.210
Everyone will be so happy!

00:17:26.050 --> 00:17:27.120
Food!

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:31.060
They're celebrating over so little?

00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:32.170
As you might suspect,

00:17:32.890 --> 00:17:34.880
the war does not go well.

00:17:35.250 --> 00:17:38.380
We've yet to engage in a major battle...

00:17:39.080 --> 00:17:42.000
But their harassment by cavalry persists day and night.

00:17:42.810 --> 00:17:44.990
The soldiers grow exhausted,

00:17:44.990 --> 00:17:48.200
and any supplies brought along the road are stolen.

00:17:48.200 --> 00:17:50.560
Barely anything is left.

00:17:50.560 --> 00:17:53.650
<i>They do look pretty thin, now that she mentions it.</i>

00:17:54.520 --> 00:17:55.650
Oh, right.

00:17:56.070 --> 00:17:58.690
I brought a letter from Oshutoru.

00:17:58.690 --> 00:18:00.280
From General Oshutoru?

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:04.540
And this is from the princess.

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:06.040
From the princess?

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:09.410
She sent this for me?

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:14.970
She said it was a national secret or something.

00:18:14.970 --> 00:18:17.920
S-S-Something like that, yes!

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:20.430
Haku-san!

00:18:21.050 --> 00:18:22.430
Haku-san!

00:18:22.930 --> 00:18:24.040
Kiuru!

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:25.450
It's been so long!

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:26.810
Have you been well?

00:18:26.810 --> 00:18:28.310
Y-Yeah.

00:18:28.310 --> 00:18:30.150
D-Did you lose some weight?

00:18:31.720 --> 00:18:33.770
Is Yamato still doing well?

00:18:33.770 --> 00:18:34.460
Yes.

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:36.140
Glad to hear it.

00:18:37.190 --> 00:18:39.210
Nekone-san!

00:18:40.170 --> 00:18:41.090
Kiuru?

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:42.590
Nekone-san!

00:18:42.590 --> 00:18:45.950
You came all this way for me, didn't you?

00:18:45.950 --> 00:18:46.660
Not really.

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:48.450
I'm so happy!

00:18:48.450 --> 00:18:52.100
You heard about our situation and were worried about me, weren't you?

00:18:52.100 --> 00:18:52.990
Not really.

00:18:52.990 --> 00:18:54.590
But everything's okay now.

00:18:54.590 --> 00:18:56.840
Seeing you has made me feel all better.

00:18:57.440 --> 00:18:59.180
It's true the situation's bad,

00:18:59.180 --> 00:19:01.400
but I'll turn it around!

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:05.350
W-W-With... the power of love!

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:09.020
I'm sorry this was all I could bring.

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:11.360
No, it's still a huge help.

00:19:12.100 --> 00:19:13.820
<i>Hold your head high, man.</i>

00:19:15.780 --> 00:19:17.050
Munechika!

00:19:17.050 --> 00:19:19.110
Is Munechika not here yet?

00:19:19.650 --> 00:19:24.120
I was just seeing to the reinforcements and supplies that arrived.

00:19:24.750 --> 00:19:25.900
I'll ask your forgiveness.

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:28.120
Munechika, you're late!

00:19:28.510 --> 00:19:29.620
Master Haku!

00:19:30.910 --> 00:19:31.950
Maro!

00:19:31.950 --> 00:19:33.120
How've you been?

00:19:34.440 --> 00:19:37.210
I'm doing just fine!

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:38.640
You're...

00:19:38.640 --> 00:19:39.880
I remember you!

00:19:40.470 --> 00:19:42.510
You're Oshutoru's servant.

00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:46.540
He'll be working under my command.

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:48.510
Please allow him to attend this conference.

00:19:49.670 --> 00:19:50.950
Let's get started.

00:19:54.160 --> 00:19:56.330
Time is finite,

00:19:56.330 --> 00:19:58.770
and more precious than any resource.

00:20:00.520 --> 00:20:05.350
In other words, since our orders come from the Emperor, what we do is righteous!

00:20:05.350 --> 00:20:08.630
Tusukuru is an isolated country at the end of the world.

00:20:08.630 --> 00:20:11.790
A worthless barbarian island!

00:20:11.790 --> 00:20:14.100
Why hesitate?

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:19.500
Once we begin in earnest, we will topple their fortress with ease.

00:20:19.500 --> 00:20:21.550
What is there to fear?

00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:26.190
A splendid speech, Dekoponpo-sama!

00:20:26.190 --> 00:20:28.380
You are indeed correct.

00:20:28.380 --> 00:20:31.590
No, the mountain where the fortress is located is steep

00:20:31.590 --> 00:20:33.400
and well-defended.

00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:38.270
I believe our best move would be to withdraw our troops and regroup.

00:20:38.270 --> 00:20:39.590
Munechika!

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:42.720
I've heard nothing but talk of retreat from you!

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:46.290
You dare defy the Emperor's will?

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:49.890
Dekoponpo, your accusation just now is not one I can afford to ignore.

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:51.450
You will rescind your words.

00:20:51.450 --> 00:20:53.410
D-Dekoponpo?

00:20:53.410 --> 00:20:55.580
How dare you address me with no title!

00:20:55.580 --> 00:21:01.320
We may both be Eight Pillar Generals, but I'm one of noble birth!

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:02.560
Know your place—

00:21:02.560 --> 00:21:03.590
Silence!

00:21:04.060 --> 00:21:05.420
You—

00:21:05.420 --> 00:21:07.210
Enough, Munechika.

00:21:08.090 --> 00:21:11.820
While that mountain of flesh is always disgusting,

00:21:11.820 --> 00:21:14.150
it's unlike you to behave so.

00:21:14.680 --> 00:21:17.030
I apologize for upsetting you.

00:21:17.030 --> 00:21:19.230
I let the blood run to my head, it seems.

00:21:19.480 --> 00:21:21.550
Then it's decided!

00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:23.880
A bold, gallant march!

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:26.940
We shall alight upon the enemy with graceful flair

00:21:26.940 --> 00:21:30.440
and take the fortress with quick, responsive tactics!

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:32.490
Splendid!

00:21:32.490 --> 00:21:34.650
That's my Dekoponpo-sama.

00:21:34.650 --> 00:21:36.370
<i>How was that splendid in any way?</i>

00:21:36.370 --> 00:21:40.640
Munechika, you'll take the vanguard.

00:21:40.640 --> 00:21:41.630
Me?

00:21:41.990 --> 00:21:45.320
You excel at defending fortresses, no?

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:48.130
Surely then, you are well-informed on how to best attack them.

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:50.760
Do as you will.

00:21:50.760 --> 00:21:57.020
But do not forget your failure with the Uzuurussha.

00:21:57.020 --> 00:22:01.020
If you fail this time, you can consider yourself finished.

00:22:01.020 --> 00:22:03.380
I-I know that.

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:06.160
I-I just need to win, don't I?

00:22:10.750 --> 00:22:11.780
Sorry about this.

00:22:12.580 --> 00:22:16.090
I'm sure you're tired from your long journey.

00:22:16.090 --> 00:22:17.790
I don't mind,

00:22:18.220 --> 00:22:19.680
but why me?

00:22:19.680 --> 00:22:23.290
One reason is to make sure you 
understand our present situation.

00:22:23.970 --> 00:22:27.920
We're at a serious disadvantage, 
yet we still can't agree on anything.

00:22:29.670 --> 00:22:30.990
The other reason

00:22:32.110 --> 00:22:36.180
is that I hope you can turn this situation around.

00:22:37.410 --> 00:22:39.740
General Oshutoru knows this well.

00:22:40.700 --> 00:22:43.940
His letter says that you will be of use.

00:22:45.060 --> 00:22:47.320
But that's not all.

00:22:48.020 --> 00:22:49.100
The princess, too.

00:22:50.410 --> 00:22:53.430
The princess changed when she met you.

00:22:53.430 --> 00:22:58.440
Now she has a smile on her face that brings joy to everyone around her.

00:22:59.310 --> 00:22:59.830
And...

00:23:06.300 --> 00:23:09.590
A steep, well-defended mountain, huh?

00:23:11.220 --> 00:23:12.070
Well...

00:23:12.070 --> 00:23:14.220
I'll come up with something.

00:23:14.820 --> 00:23:17.720
But I'd appreciate it if you didn't expect too much.

00:23:20.410 --> 00:23:23.350
You're the first person to say such a thing to me.
